  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023-SHF Reserve for Emergencies- Flexible live-saving response to conflict-affected people in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to minimize the health and Nutrition impacts of humanitarian and public health emergencies through the provision _x000d_
of immediate life-saving activities, strengthening of service delivery &amp; improve access to quality health services to people in need _x000d_
(PIN) specifically for those who are affected by armed conflict and other vulnerabilities such as People with Disabilities (PWD), _x000d_
Internally displaced people (IDPs) and host communities in White Nile (WN) State.Plan International will address the urgent needs by supporting the provision of free accessible quality lifesaving health services in _x000d_
the targeted localities of Rabak, Kosti, Al Salam, Edwin and Aljebelain targeting 53750 IDPs (about 30% of total 179782 IDPs in _x000d_
these locations) and 5374 people from the host communities. We will work with health authorities including the State Ministry of _x000d_
Health (SMOH) to ensure availability of medical supplies and qualified health cadre and healthcare workers and build their _x000d_
capacity to promptly respond to health needs of the targeted population. We will ensure the availability of life saving medications _x000d_
and supplies, supporting the improvement of the infrastructure of the health facilities and enhancing reporting mechanisms by _x000d_
expanding the reporting capacity of the early warning systems and strengthen emergency preparedness through the provision _x000d_
of phone credit cards and printing of protocols for reporting format in the localities. The project aims to support vulnerable _x000d_
people by providing logistical support to 2 health clinics in AL Jazira Aba &amp; Shabasha and 2 mobile clinics in Knana &amp; Eldueim in _x000d_
Al Jabalin &amp; Eldueim localities, the service will include: outpatient consultation (OPD) communicable and non-communicable _x000d_
disease, treatment of injuries, EPI services, reproductive health services including: ANC, PNC, Family planning services and _x000d_
also providing clinical management of Gender Based Violence (GBV) survivors._x000d_
The service will also extend to provide referral of complicated emergency or critical cases from the localities clinics to secondary _x000d_
and tertiary care, Plan will provide transport, medical services, and support the cost of accommodation and meals for the referral _x000d_
of emergency obstetric services. This will target 250 pregnant women and 80 children with severe acute malnutrition. _x000d_
Awareness/orientation sessions at the health facility on community and personal health and hygiene, floods and diseases outbreak _x000d_
preparedness and responses will also be conducted in the localities.</narrative>
  </description>
